const e={readingNotes:[{title:{zh:"研究问题",en:"Research question"},body:{zh:"论文考察加入盈利能力和投资因子的五因子框架如何组织若干平均收益异象。 阅读时先把它理解为一个被界定的问题，而不是可以脱离样本、时间和制度环境的结论。",en:"“Dissecting Anomalies with a Five-Factor Model” frames a bounded research question. Read the stated question together with the named sample, dates, and institutional setting rather than treating it as a conclusion that automatically travels to another market or period."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1093/rfs/hhv043",label:{zh:"Review of Financial Studies (2016) · 来源说明",en:"Review of Financial Studies (2016) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"研究设计",en:"Research design"},body:{zh:"来源将特征组合回报与五因子暴露放在同一模型中，比较不同异象在该规格下的解释情况。 这说明比较对象、观察窗口和对照关系是研究合同的一部分；改变其中任何一项，都可能改变所检验的命题。",en:"For “Dissecting Anomalies with a Five-Factor Model”, the source describes a deliberate comparison, observation window, and control relation. Those choices are part of its research contract: changing one can change the proposition being tested, even when the method label remains the same."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1093/rfs/hhv043",label:{zh:"Review of Financial Studies (2016) · 来源说明",en:"Review of Financial Studies (2016) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"数据与时点",en:"Data and timing"},body:{zh:"需要因子定义、特征组合、复权收益、形成规则、样本成员和会计信息的可得时点。 数据字段、可得时点和样本筛选需要与原始研究分开记录，不能仅凭同名变量或最终修订数据就视为可比。",en:"For “Dissecting Anomalies with a Five-Factor Model”, keep the fields, their availability timing, and the sample filters separate from the original study. A same-named variable, later-revised database, or matching end-of-period date is not automatically a comparable input."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1093/rfs/hhv043",label:{zh:"Review of Financial Studies (2016) · 来源说明",en:"Review of Financial Studies (2016) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"如何理解结果",en:"How to read the result"},body:{zh:"摘要讨论若干异象与因子暴露的共同解释，而不是宣称五因子模型消除了所有异象或保证未来溢价。 它支持的是该来源所描述的经验或理论关系；它本身不把相关性、模型拟合或历史表现升级为因果、可执行性或未来保证。",en:"For “Dissecting Anomalies with a Five-Factor Model”, the source supports only the empirical or theoretical relation it describes. It does not turn association, model fit, or historical performance into causality, a directly executable procedure, or a guarantee about subsequent outcomes."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1093/rfs/hhv043",label:{zh:"Review of Financial Studies (2016) · 来源说明",en:"Review of Financial Studies (2016) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"复核清单",en:"Replication checks"},body:{zh:"冻结因子构造、再平衡和断点，纳入退市证券，按披露可得性对齐会计变量，并记录市场和时期。 在做后续分析前，应把这些选择写入版本化的研究记录，并保留原始来源链接与访问日期。",en:"Before extending “Dissecting Anomalies with a Five-Factor Model”, record its sample, timing, construction choices, and source edition in a versioned note. Keep the primary-source link and access date so a later reader can distinguish a changed definition from a changed result."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1093/rfs/hhv043",label:{zh:"Review of Financial Studies (2016) · 来源说明",en:"Review of Financial Studies (2016) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"适用边界",en:"Scope boundary"},body:{zh:"该条导读引用 Review of Financial Studies (2016)。历史因子拟合不等于当前可获得回报；融资、卖空、交易成本和市场制度仍须单独评估。 若需要量化结论、参数、表格或稳健性检验，请回到原文并单独核对版本、附录与样本定义。",en:"This guide cites Review of Financial Studies (2016) for “Dissecting Anomalies with a Five-Factor Model”. Its public description defines the boundary. For numerical conclusions, parameters, tables, or robustness tests, return to the original and separately verify the edition, appendices, and sample definitions."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1093/rfs/hhv043",label:{zh:"Review of Financial Studies (2016) · 来源说明",en:"Review of Financial Studies (2016) · source description"}}}],readerLimits:{zh:"本文只整理“Dissecting Anomalies with a Five-Factor Model”所公开说明的研究问题与设计边界，不构成收益预测、交易规则或全文复现。历史因子拟合不等于当前可获得回报；融资、卖空、交易成本和市场制度仍须单独评估。",en:"This guide only organizes the publicly described question and design of “Dissecting Anomalies with a Five-Factor Model”. It is not a return forecast, trading rule, or full-text replication. The source's stated scope remains controlling."}};export{e as default};
